-- title:
--   Base-changed automorphism preserves each component of the geometric fibre
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$ and $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\ L$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield generated by the image, under the coefficientwise map [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero with image in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\ L$ the series [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81). Write $X =$ [`ModularCurve.TwoChartModel A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L229), the pushout of the two charts $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the integral closures of $A[j]$ and $A[j^{-1}]$ in $K$, with structure morphism [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) to $\mathrm{Spec}\ A$ and chart immersion [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.ιFin`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L231) from $X^{\mathrm{Fin}} = \mathrm{Spec}$ of `chartAlgFin`, whose open range is `chartFinOpen`. Let $\sigma$ be a self-isomorphism of $X$ with $\sigma$ followed by `modelTo` equal to `modelTo`, and $\rho$ a ring endomorphism of `chartAlgFin` with $\mathrm{Spec}(\rho)$ followed by `ιFin` equal to `ιFin` followed by $\sigma.\mathrm{hom}$. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field which is an $A$-algebra, and form the fibre $X_k = X \times_{\mathrm{Spec}\ A} \mathrm{Spec}\ k$ with first projection $\mathrm{pr}_1$. Assume: (a) for every irreducible component $Z$ of the space of $X_k$, its generic point lies in $\mathrm{pr}_1^{-1}(\mathrm{chartFinOpen})$; (b) for every such $Z$ and every point $y$ of $X^{\mathrm{Fin}}$ with $\iota^{\mathrm{Fin}}(y) = \mathrm{pr}_1(\eta_Z)$, the prime of $y$ satisfies $\rho^{-1}(y) = y$; (c) any two components admitting a common such $y$ are equal. Then for every irreducible component $Z$ of $X_k$, the base map of `curveChange σ.hom hσ (specMap A k)`, the base change of $\sigma$ along $\mathrm{Spec}\ k \to \mathrm{Spec}\ A$, carries $Z$ onto $Z$.
--
--   This is the topological step in showing that an automorphism of the integral two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$ over $A$ — in the application a diamond operator at $p$ — stabilises each irreducible component of the geometric special fibre individually, in the style of the analysis of the fibre of modular curves at $p$. It feeds the statements about diamond automorphisms and the components of the special fibre of the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$.
